.TH df 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
df \- report filesystem space
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B df
[\fB\-ikf\fR] [\fIpath\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B df
prints, for each mounted filesystem, its total size, how much is used
and how much is free.  Given one or more
.IR path s,
it reports only the filesystems those paths are on.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-i
Report inodes rather than blocks.  Worth remembering: a FUZIX filesystem
can run out of inodes with blocks to spare, and the failure looks like a
full disk.
.TP
.B \-k
Report kilobytes rather than 512-byte blocks.
.TP
.B \-f
Show the percentage free rather than the percentage used.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# df
# df -k
# df -i
# df /root
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR du (1),
.BR mount (1),
.BR free (1)
